                      # Internet Not Working #

## Scenario / Issue
Users could not access the internet despite an active network connection.  
- Webpages wouldn’t load in any browser  
- Other apps could not connect  
- Network icon: “No Internet” or “Limited Connectivity”

## Root Causes Considered
- DNS misconfiguration  
- Cached bad DNS entries  
- Network adapter misconfigured, disabled, or driver issue  
- IP conflict / incorrect network settings

## Troubleshooting Steps
1. Verified physical connection (Wi-Fi/Ethernet)  
2. Checked other devices on network  
3. Ran "ipconfig /all" - confirmed IP, subnet, gateway, DNS  
4. Tested connectivity:
   - Ping localhost, gateway, external IP ("8.8.8.8")  
   - Ping domain name ("google.com")  
   - Ran "nslookup google.com"  
5. Flushed DNS cache ("ipconfig /flushdns")  
6. Reset network stack ("netsh winsock reset")  
7. Updated/reinstalled network adapter driver (if needed)

## Findings
- IP assigned correctly  
- Gateway reachable  
- Could ping external IP, but DNS resolution failed  
- Local DNS misconfigured / cached bad entries

## Resolution
- Flushed DNS and reset network stack - restored domain resolution  
- Updated network adapter driver - ensured stable connection

## Outcome
Internet access restored, DNS resolving correctly, network adapter fully functional.
